KNOWNBUG: N5008 [temp.arg.explicit] + [temp.deduct]/2 -- a call supplying
only explicit template arguments to an OVERLOADED member function
template, appearing as the initializer of a DEFAULT TEMPLATE ARGUMENT of
another member template (libstdc++ <tuple>'s
`bool _Valid = __valid_args<_UElements...>()` forwarding-constructor
shape), finds no viable overload; the enclosing constructor is removed
from the overload set and resolution fails ("found no match").  The same
call resolves fine when made directly, and a non-overloaded callee works
in the same default-argument position -- the broken ingredient is
overload selection by explicit template arguments inside the
default-template-argument context.  In real libstdc++ this silently drops
tuple's perfect-forwarding constructors (masked whenever
`tuple(const _Elements&...)` also matches).  Header-free; g++/clang++
runtime-verified.  Flip to CORE when fixed.
